-- Generated by tools/make_news.py from CHANGELOG.md. Do not edit by hand.
local _, TCF = ...
TCF.NEWS = {
  { version = "1.7.3", highlight = nil, text = "- The \"Your spot\" tag and gold frame over your newest gathering spot are gone.\n- Tooltips and the recipe list no longer say how likely a skill point is (\"always\", \"often\" and so on), since the chance changed and the words were wrong. The colours still show it, and you see your skill go up in the bar.\n\n|cffffd100Finding things|r\n- A new Materials page in the Compendium lists every material in the game with where it comes from (which gathering spot, rare find, daily craft, garden, fishing or cooking) and what it's used in. It has a search box.\n- Recipe tooltips say where to get any material you're short on, and so does the Profession Bag.\n- The Item Sets page now starts with the cosmetic sets: the 11 legendary crafted sets (with their profession) and the dungeon sets. Click one to see its pieces and try them on.\n- The recipe list has a Sets button that shows only set recipes, so the legendary sets are easy to find." },
  { version = "1.7.2", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Gathering spots make sense now|r\n- Spots open one after another. Own at least one of a spot to open the next one; a spot you own always stays open. The later spots still need their Renown, skill or Trade Gold too.\n- Your spot (the newest one you own) has a gold frame and a \"Your spot\" tag. The next one to buy says so.\n- The spot list turns in whole pages (spots 1 to 6, then 7 to 9), so no spot shows up on two pages.\n- Glints and stashes only come up on the page you're looking at. One on a page you leave ends quietly.\n\n|cffffd100Guild work orders|r\n- When you have the materials, a Craft button beside the order makes the gear it wants (or today's daily material) right there. A Masterwork counts for the order too.\n\n|cffffd100Recipe search|r\n- The recipe list has a search box: type part of an item's or set's name.\n\n|cffffd100Item Sets in the Compendium|r\n- Every set says where it comes from: the Adventure zones and bosses (MC, BWL, ZG, Strat...), the raid chests, or world drops. The list has a short tag, the tooltip the full list.\n- Click a set to see its pieces below the list. Click a piece to try it on, or Try on all for the whole set. Shift-click a set in the list does the same." },
  { version = "1.7.1", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Work orders fix|r\n- A work order can no longer ask for more of a material than your bag can hold. Orders now ask for at most three quarters of your bag's stack size (no limit with the Bottomless Bag).\n- Orders already on your board that were too big now ask for what fits, with the same reward.\n- You can deliver part of an order: hand in what you have now and bring the rest later. The reward comes when the whole order is in.\n\n|cffffd100Rare drops list|r\n- Each profession's Help guide now lists its rare drops, where they come from and how often:\n  - Mining, Skinning and Cloth Scavenging: the rare finds and the spots that give them.\n  - Herbalism: the rare herbs and the seeds they come with.\n  - Fishing: Mr. Pinchy and treasure chests.\n- On the Guild page, hover the rare finds line for the same list.\n\n|cffffd100Taps|r\n- The auto-clicker guard is now a short pause. A key or mouse button pressed at a machine-steady rhythm stops counting for 10 seconds, then counts again. Before, it could stay paused until the rhythm changed or you reloaded." },
  { version = "1.7.0", highlight = "Professions 2.0: rare finds and glints by hand, named helpers, guilds with work orders, specializations, a Renown shop, a Profession Bag and 11 legendary crafted sets.", text = "|cffffd100Professions 2.0: a reason to work your spots by hand|r\n- The \"By hand\" buttons no longer show your tool's level on every row.\n- Rare finds: clicking a gathering spot by hand can find something rare, better at the later spots. Ore: Black Diamond, Star Ruby, Blood of the Mountain. Leather: Warbear Leather, Black Dragonscale, Pristine Hide of the Beast. Cloth: Essence of Undeath, Demonic Rune, Righteous Orb. Helpers never find them.\n- Glints: now and then a spot's tool sparkles. Click it by hand in time for 5 times the reward and a combo; every glint in a row makes rare finds likelier.\n- Spot events while you watch your spots: a stash to grab with 10 quick clicks, a rich spot that pays 3 times as much for 30 seconds, or a patrol to hide from (don't click, and your helpers work twice as fast for a minute).\n- Your helpers have names and traits now, and bring more goods as they level up, all the way to level 20.\n- The gathering spots show your materials exactly (701,620 Linen Cloth instead of 701.62K) up to 10 million, so every click shows.\n\n|cffffd100Professions 2.0: deeper layers (the new Guild page)|r\n- Specializations at 225, like Classic: Mooncloth, Shadoweave or Spellfire Tailoring, Armorsmith or Weaponsmith, Dragonscale or Tribal Leatherworking. Each has its own perk and daily craft (Primal Mooncloth, Shadowcloth, Spellcloth, Enchanted Thorium, Arcanite, Cured Rugged Hide, Enchanted Leather).\n- Guilds and work orders: The Silken Thread, the Thorium Brotherhood and the Hide and Hunt Lodge post orders for materials, crafted gear, rare finds and daily materials. Orders pay Trade Gold, TapCoins and reputation, from Initiate to Grand Master. Grand Master comes with a title.\n- Masterwork: crafted gear now and then comes out as a Masterwork version with better stats.\n- Renown shop: selling your business also gives Renown points. Spend them on perks that stay forever: Sharp Tools, Keen Eye, Glint Seeker, Busy Hands, Guild Ties, Rested Hands and Steady Hands. Cats that already have Renown start with points.\n- Titles: click your cat's title in the window to show one you earned.\n\n|cffffd100Renown and unlocks|r\n- Herbalism, First Aid, Fishing and Cooking now open with the Trade Gold your cat earned since its last sale, not all the Trade Gold it ever earned. Selling your business closes them again until you earn it back, which goes faster with every bit of Renown. Your garden, skills, potions and the rest are kept for when they open again.\n- Gathering skill (Mining, Skinning, Cloth Scavenging) rises a third as fast now, and starts over when you sell. With this patch every cat keeps a third of its gathering skill. Your best skill ever still counts for opening the later spots, and spots you already opened stay open.\n- The Renown page says plainly what selling does to your money: your bonus now, your bonus after selling, and how much more money that is.\n\n|cffffd100Profession Bag|r\n- A new Bag button on the Professions page shows every material your cat has, by tab (Gathered, Rare, Daily, Herbs, Fish & Food, Bandages). Hover one to see what it's used for, and shift-click to sell a whole stack for Trade Gold.\n- Bags hold stacks of a set size: a Linen Bag holds 20,000 of each. Every kind always fits, and anything past the size is sold for Trade Gold right away, so nothing is wasted. Piles you already have stay as they are.\n- Buy bigger bags with TapCoins, all the way from the Wool Bag to the Bottomless Bag (no limit at all). Bags count for all your cats.\n\n|cffffd100TapCoins|r\n- The TapCoin is orange now, so it doesn't look like Trade Gold.\n- A gentle auto-clicker guard: if one key is pressed at a perfectly steady, machine-like rhythm for a long run, it stops counting until the rhythm changes. Nothing is taken away, and fast mashing by a real person never trips it.\n\n|cffffd100Legendary profession sets|r\n- 11 new animated sets you craft over a long time. Tailoring: Mooncloth Regalia (moonlight and stars), Felweave Shroud (fel fire) and Spellfire (arcane flames). Blacksmithing: Sulfuron Forgemaster (a molten forge) and Dark Iron Bulwark (smouldering dark iron). Leatherworking: Black Dragonscale and Devilsaur Hunter. Herbalism: Lotus Bloom. Fishing: Pinchy's Wish. Cooking: Feast of the Ages. First Aid: Field Medic.\n- Their titles: Moonweaver, Felweaver, Spellfire Savant, Forgemaster, Dark Iron Warden, Dragonscale Stalker, Devilsaur Hunter, Lotus Keeper, Angler of Legend, Master Chef and Field Medic.\n- Each set takes a long time on purpose: skill 300, your specialization, a high guild rank, many daily materials and rare finds. Owning a whole set gives its title." },
  { version = "1.6.8", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Tapping faces|r\n- Your cat's face now changes the longer and faster you tap, through ten faces: Keen, Perky, Focused, Determined, Excited, Sweating, Intense, Starstruck, On fire and Legendary. Its cheeks go redder as it gets more worked up.\n- It takes both speed and staying power: a quick burst only gets the first few faces, and Legendary takes a long run of fast tapping. Slow down and it calms back down one face at a time.\n\n|cffffd100Petting faces|r\n- While you pet your cat, it goes through ten cute faces as you get closer to Happy Purrs: Curious, Pleased, Shy, Cosy, Purring, Smitten, Melty, Lovestruck, Blissful and, when it starts to purr, Pure love. Kawaii blush included.\n\n|cffffd100Settings|r\n- New \"Tapping and petting faces\" box, on by default. Turn it off to keep your cat's calm face." },
  { version = "1.6.7", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd10018 new pet effects|r\n- Full-colour ones this time: Fireballs, Crackling Lightning, Poison Drips, Frost Shards, Shadow Wisps, Holy Light, Arcane Runes, Fel Fire and Blood Drops, plus Yarn Balls, Fishies, Toy Mice, Catnip, Butterflies, Little Ghosts, Moons, Crowns and Gems.\n- Like the others, they come from Happy Purrs with your cat: Yarn Balls on a second day, Fireballs on the 10th, Crackling Lightning after 10 days in a row, all the way to Gems for a whole year. The Compendium shows what each one needs, and days you already have count.\n\n|cffffd100Herbalism, much deeper|r\n- Every plot keeps its own seed now. Pick a seed and right-click a plot to grow it there from the next harvest on (a small icon shows what comes next), shift-right-click to dig it up and plant it now, or use \"Grow it in every plot\". Your gardener finally follows along, so you can change what grows without losing your gardener.\n- Meet Bramble, your gardener. Hire it, then train it from Apprentice to Journeyman, Expert, Artisan and Master: plants grow faster, one replant in three is free, one more herb from every harvest, and twice the rare herbs. Bramble also plants empty plots for you. All of this has its own Gardener page next to Garden.\n- 18 more herbs from the real game, 26 in all: Earthroot, Stranglekelp, Bruiseweed, Wild Steelbloom, Liferoot, Goldthorn, Khadgar's Whisker, Wintersbite, Firebloom, Purple Lotus, Arthas' Tears, Blindweed, Ghost Mushroom, Gromsblood, Golden Sansam, Mountain Silversage, Plaguebloom and Icecap. Use the arrows (or the mouse wheel) to page through the seeds.\n- Rare herbs come with some harvests: Swiftthistle from Mageroyal or Briarthorn, Wildvine from Firebloom, Purple Lotus or Gromsblood, and Black Lotus from Sungrass, Dreamfoil and the high herbs.\n- New garden upgrades: Rain Barrel (watering helps three times as much), Alchemy Lab (potions last twice as long) and Moonwell (twice the rare herbs).\n\n|cffffd100Potions|r\n- Herbalism's Crafting list now brews 17 potions from your herbs, from Elixir of Lion's Strength to Flask of the Titans, Flask of Supreme Power and Flask of Distilled Wisdom (those need a Black Lotus).\n- Drink one for a buff: Adventure damage or health, cat XP, gathering profits, rare fish or garden growth. One potion at a time, and it counts on top of a Well Fed dish. Brewing raises your Herbalism skill too.\n\n|cffffd100Rock paper scissors: best of 3 and best of 5|r\n- A new button in the top bar picks best of 1, 3 or 5, against the house cat or a friend. In best of 3 the first to win 2 rounds takes the game, in best of 5 the first to win 3. Ties still play again and don't count.\n- The score shows in the top bar while the game runs, and each round won gets a small cheer. The bet is the same for the whole game: one bet, one payout.\n- Your friend needs this version for best of 3 or 5 (the game tells you if they don't have it yet). Best of 1 works with every version.\n\n|cffffd100Crafting|r\n- The button next to Craft now says how many it makes (\"x12\", \"x50\") instead of \"All\", since one click makes at most 50.\n\n|cffffd100Settings|r\n- New Show party cats box: turn it off to hide the row of party members' cats beside yours. It only hides the picture: your taps still count more with friends, and death roll, rock paper scissors and party expeditions still work." },
  { version = "1.6.6", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Happy Purrs|r\n- Pet your cat (left-click it on your screen, or its picture in the window) 100 times in a row and it purrs: +5% XP for an hour. While it purrs, 50 pets in a row start the hour again. A short pause between pets is fine.\n- Each class's cat purrs on its own. While it purrs, a tiny heart sits next to its XP bar, and a heart next to the class name in the window lights up (hover it for how it works and how many pets you're on).\n\n|cffffd100Pet effects|r\n- A new Pet Effect slot in Appearance: what floats up when you pet your cat, in place of the hearts. Paw Prints, Purr Notes, Little Stars, Bubbles, Falling Leaves, Purr Sparkles, Snowflakes, Lucky Coins and Rainbow Hearts.\n- They come from being there for your cat: Happy Purrs on more days, and on more days in a row, with that cat. The Compendium shows what each one needs." },
  { version = "1.6.5", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Gear that fits your class, like WoW|r\n- Equip best, the green and red Power numbers on the Gear page, gear tooltips and the loot box now judge gear by what each class really needs. Mages, Warlocks and Priests go for Spell Power and Intellect (Priests also Spirit), Warriors and Paladins for Strength, Hunters and Rogues for Agility, and Shamans and Druids for what they fight with, spells or weapons. Stamina still helps every cat, but no longer wins over a class's main stats.\n- Intellect, Spirit and mana regeneration on a caster's gear now add to its spell damage, and Power counts critical hits.\n- Gear that drops for you now and then matches your class's stats a little better too: Stamina-only pieces no longer count as caster gear.\n- Adventure enemies have 6% more health, so the stronger, better-chosen gear keeps zones as long as before, and Power is sized as before, so expeditions are as hard as they were.\n\n|cffffd100Realm leaderboard|r\n- Extra rows that the two-word name problem of 1.6.1.1 left behind (a player listed again under part of someone's name, like \"Its Caffeinated-Trip\" or \"Ziggu-Trip\") are removed and not taken in again, so each player shows once.\n- The \"still being worked on\" note is gone: the leaderboard works." },
  { version = "1.6.4", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Death roll with a friend: no more /reload|r\n- If it's your friend's turn and their roll hasn't come through for 20 seconds, the button turns into Call off: it ends the duel and both bets come back, so you can start the next one at once.\n- No more waiting after the 1: each side settles the moment it sees the 1 roll (the loser pays, the winner is paid), and the next duel can start straight away." },
  { version = "1.6.3", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Try things on|r\n- Shift-click an item to try it on your cat: gear on the Gear page, cosmetics and skins on the Appearance page, the Shop's offers and your racial accessory, crafting recipes, and anything in the Compendium (it opens the main window). It stays on your cat while you look around, so you can put a hat and a cape together. Shift-click it again to take it off, or press Clear preview under your cat. Nothing is equipped or bought.\n- The tooltips say \"Shift-click to try it on your cat.\" Closing the window or switching class takes the previewed items off." },
  { version = "1.6.2", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Phone view|r\n- Everything is bigger: the phone view is a little wider and every page in it is drawn larger, so text is easier to read and buttons are easier to hit.\n- New Tabs button next to the Compendium in the phone view: fold the two rows of round page buttons into one menu button, so the pages get more room. Click the menu to pick a page, or click Tabs again to get the round buttons back. Your choice is remembered.\n\n|cffffd100Header|r\n- Achievements and Settings now sit right after the Compendium, and the whole row (character, phone view, Compendium, Achievements, Settings) stays in the same place when you fold the character panel away or open it again.\n- Very large TapCoin amounts show in short form at the top of the window (1.25M).\n\n|cffffd100Gear|r\n- With no spare gear, the note about where gear comes from now sits in the middle of the list and wraps, instead of running across the whole window behind Sell junk and Equip best.\n\n|cffffd100Professions|r\n- The x3 upgrades now multiply the goods a spot gathers (ore, leather, cloth) as well as its Trade Gold, and Renown adds its 2% a point to goods too. The upgrades are now called \"Trade Gold and goods x3\".\n- The Buy and Hire buttons on every spot are taller and easier to click, and Hire shows just the price (\"Hire 75.00K\") so it fits on one line. Hover it to see who you hire.\n- The profession icons and the page buttons under them are a little bigger." },
  { version = "1.6.1.2", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Realm leaderboard: one row per player|r\n- On World of Warcraft: Forever the game tells an addon only the first word of a two-word character name and hands it the second word as the realm, so your own addon called you \"Ziggu\" on realm \"Trip\" while your friends' addons saw \"Ziggu Trip\". The leaderboard now uses the name the game puts on your messages, the one everyone else sees, and no longer takes the second word of your name for the realm. Boards with two rows for the same player (\"Its Caffeinated\" and \"Its-Caffeinated\") are tidied: the row under the split name is recognised as that player's and merged, even while they are still on an older version.\n- Your summary only goes out once your addon knows the name the game uses for you (a moment after joining a group), so nothing is shared under a half name.\n- The title no longer shows a stand-in realm name." },
  { version = "1.6.1.1", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Realm leaderboard: names with a space|r\n- World of Warcraft: Forever lets a character name have a space in it (\"Ziggu Trip\"). The leaderboard refused every message from such a player, so friends never showed up on each other's boards even though their cats and taps showed in the party row. Names with a space now count everywhere on the leaderboard, and a row saved under a wrong name for your own character is cleaned up.\n- When the game gives no realm name, the leaderboard no longer takes the second word of your name for the realm." },
  { version = "1.6.1", highlight = nil, text = "Fixes for the multiplayer problems players reported in 1.6.0. Multiplayer is still in the works, and we would like to hear whether the death roll works for you now (/tcf feedback).\n\n|cffffd100Casino: death roll and rock paper scissors with a friend|r\n- A death roll or rock paper scissors game with a friend no longer stops with \"is no longer in your group\" right after the challenge is accepted. The game hides the group's names from addons, so TapCatForever no longer asks the game whether your friend is still there: it knows from your friend's own addon. Your friend counts as gone only when their addon has been quiet and the group has really changed, with a few seconds of grace. When the game does show your friend's name in the group, that confirms they are there.\n- A friend on a loading screen (a hearth, a portal, a zone line) no longer ends the game: the game reports them as offline for a moment, and the same few seconds of grace apply before the game is called off and the bets come back.\n- A roll result the game hides from the addon now calls the death roll off with your bet back, instead of waiting for the turn timer.\n\n|cffffd100Party cats|r\n- A friend's profile (click their cat in the party row) now shows their total taps, achievements, zones cleared and whether they are on the leaderboard, above their gear.\n- Party cats tell each other their stats along with their look, at most once a minute and only when something changed. Older versions ignore the extra information. A cat wearing many long-named crafted cosmetics sends its gear first and leaves out what does not fit, so nothing that 1.6.0 showed goes missing because of the stats.\n\n|cffffd100Realm leaderboard|r\n- The leaderboard fills in from the players in your party or raid: a friend who has joined the leaderboard shows up on yours (and you on theirs) as soon as you see their cat in the party row. Players who have not joined stay off the board, and a friend who leaves the leaderboard comes off yours the same way.\n- Your own row never stays in the saved board under your name when one of your own party messages comes back before the addon knows your name (after a /reload).\n- /tcf lbdebug now also says how many rows came from party messages and why messages were dropped. Send it to the developer if players still don't show up.\n\n|cffffd100Other|r\n- The What's new box's Read the full patch notes button opens the notes of the version the box is about; the 1.6.1 notes sit beside them." },
  { version = "1.6.0", highlight = "New: the cat Casino, a main window you can resize or make compact, professions that level like WoW, and animated cosmetic sets from Adventure's dungeons.", text = "Multiplayer is still in the works: party death roll, rock paper scissors and the leaderboard may not work yet.\n\n|cffffd100Your cats on every character|r\n- Your cats are now shared by all your characters: each class has one cat for your whole account. Any character plays the account's cat of its class (or the one you pick), with its level, XP, gear and bags, Treasure Bag, professions, look and cosmetics, Adventure progress and farming, abilities and expeditions.\n- The first time you log in on 1.6, the cats of all your characters are put together, so nothing is lost. For each class the cat with the highest level (then the most XP) keeps its level, XP, worn gear, look and place in Adventure.\n- The other cats of that class add their bag items (with the gear they wore), unopened chests, cosmetics, materials, Adventure kills and abilities. Professions keep the business with the most Trade Gold earned, the best skill in each profession and the best Renown.\n- Unopened chests were kept per character before 1.6. Every character's chests, also those of characters you no longer play, go to the cat that character was playing, at that cat's level.\n- Trade Gold earned by the businesses that weren't kept still counts toward the Trade Gold achievements and the leaderboard (not toward unlocking professions).\n- Expeditions under way on all your characters keep going. If there are more than two, the Expeditions page shows the ones back first and says how many more are under way. A second party expedition waits until the first is claimed, and its cats count as away until then.\n- One chat line says so, once. A copy of every character's old cats is kept in your saved data.\n- A character that logs in later with cats of its own (for example one you played on an older version) is put together the same way.\n- A new character starts on the account's cat of its class.\n- Still per character: which cat it plays, the Shop's Daily Wares, real WoW dungeon and raid chest limits, and how many times you killed a real WoW boss. TapCoins, quests, achievements and settings were already shared.\n- \"Reset this character\" in Settings is now \"Reset your cats\": it starts all nine cats over, for every character. TapCoins, quests and achievements are kept.\n\n|cffffd100Casino|r\n- New: the Casino (a new tab between Shop and Leaderboard), with Lucky Paws slots, blackjack, and death roll and rock paper scissors against a house cat or a friend in your party. It fills the whole window under the tabs: pick Slots, Blackjack or Death roll with the buttons at the top (the Death roll view also plays rock paper scissors).\n- In the Friend view a short line under the top bar says whether the friend you picked can play: \"Ready to play\", \"Checking their TapCatForever...\" or \"Their TapCatForever didn't answer (they need the newest version)\". Party cats work on older versions too, so you can see a friend's cat while their addon can't take a challenge yet.\n- Challenges between friends now reach the right player even when the game doesn't let addons read your own name: each addon learns the name the game gives you from your own messages.\n- Right after you join a group your addon may not know your name yet: a challenge then says so, and works a few seconds later.\n- The Casino's hellos between addons are kept to one hello and at most one answer each when the group changes, so they never hold up duel messages in a big raid.\n- /tcf name says whether the game lets addons read your name and which name TapCatForever learned for you.\n- The line at the top shows your bet limits, and your stats for the game you are playing: games played, total bet, paid back, net and your biggest win (hover it for every game).\n\n|cffffd100Casino: bets|r\n- A bet is at least 10 TapCoins and at most half your TapCoins (rounded down to the bet step). There is no top bet. You need at least 20 TapCoins to play.\n- The - and + buttons take bigger steps on big bets (100 from 1,000, 250 from 2,500, 500 from 5,000, and so on).\n- In a duel with a friend, each of you can bet at most half your own TapCoins, and exactly the bet you both agreed moves between you.\n- Big bets show in short in the bet box, for example 125.5K or 4.5M.\n- Use the - and + buttons or the quick 10, 50, 100 and Max buttons to choose your bet. All the games share the same bet, and it is kept for next time.\n- Every game against the house keeps a small house edge, so over time the Casino takes a few TapCoins out of the game. Duels with friends are even: no table fee. It is for fun, not for getting rich. There are no free spins.\n- Casino bets and wins don't count toward the TapCoins earned and spent achievements.\n\n|cffffd100Casino: Lucky Paws slots|r\n- A cartoon cat slot machine with three reels. Pull the lever or press Spin. The reels spin, slow down and stop from left to right with a little bounce. Click the reels (or press Stop) to land them at once.\n- Only the middle line counts. Three of a kind wins, and every cat on the line pays something.\n- Pays (times your bet, your bet included): three cats 100, three gems 40, three bells 25, three coins 15, three fish 10, three yarn balls 5, three paws 3, two cats 5, one cat 2.\n- The rarer a line, the more it pays: three cats come up about 1 in 1,000 spins, gems 1 in 667, bells 1 in 500, coins 1 in 400, fish 1 in 296, yarn balls 1 in 222 and paws 1 in 178. Hover the \"How it works\" line for the chance of every line.\n- The result line says what you won on top of your bet: \"One cat. You win 10 TapCoins\" on a bet of 10 (you get 20 back).\n- About 3 spins in 10 win something. Over many spins the machine pays back about 94% of what is bet.\n- A big win (10 times your bet or more) gets a coin shower, flashing lights and a cheer from your cat, inside the window only.\n\n|cffffd100Casino: blackjack|r\n- Get closer to 21 than the dealer without going over. Picture cards count 10, aces 1 or 11.\n- A win pays 1 to 1. A blackjack (an ace and a 10 card as your first two cards) pays 3 to 2, with half a TapCoin rounded down on odd bets. A tie is a push: you get your bet back.\n- The dealer draws to 17 and stands on every 17, soft 17 too. The dealer checks for blackjack first.\n- Double: double your bet on any first two cards and take exactly one more card. Split: split a pair into two hands once. Split aces get one card each.\n- No insurance. Six decks, shuffled again when a quarter of the shoe is left. With perfect play the house keeps about half a percent.\n- Closing the window doesn't lose your hand: it waits for you, even after a reload. A win is always paid, even if you close the window while the cards are still being dealt.\n\n|cffffd100Casino: death roll|r\n- Two cats take turns rolling. The first roll is 1 to 1,000 (or 100, or 10,000: pick where the rolls start). Each next roll is 1 to the last number rolled. Whoever rolls a 1 loses.\n- It plays out in a cosy cartoon cat tavern, by the fire: your cat on the left in its real look, the other cat on the right. Each roll pops up over the roller's head and the range in the middle shrinks. Numbers of 10 and below turn red and shake.\n- On a 1 the loser spins and flops onto its back with X eyes, a little ghost cat floats up, and a few seconds later it pops back up, fine. The winner jumps around in confetti.\n- A small How to play box above the table explains the rules (hover it to read them as a tooltip too).\n\n|cffffd100Casino: death roll against the house cat|r\n- Press House cat, choose your bet and where the rolls start, and press Start. The house cat has a fun name and look each game (Lucky Paws is a tuxedo cat).\n- A coin flip decides who rolls first, so you win half the games.\n- A win gives you 1.9 times your bet back: on a bet of 100 you win 90. Over many games the house keeps about 5% of what is bet.\n- A game you leave halfway waits for you, even after a reload.\n\n|cffffd100Casino: death roll with a friend|r\n- Group up (party or raid) with a friend who has TapCatForever. Press Friend, pick them with the arrows, choose a bet and press Challenge.\n- Your friend gets a small Accept or Decline box just above their cat on the screen, and in the Casino tab. It goes away after 60 seconds. If you decline or don't answer, that friend can challenge you again after 20 seconds.\n- You both need enough TapCoins for the bet (each player's own limits count). Your bet is held while the duel runs and comes back if it is called off.\n- The rolls are real /roll rolls: the Roll button rolls for you, and they also show in chat for your group like a normal /roll. You can type /roll yourself too, as long as it is your turn and the right range.\n- Whoever rolls the 1 loses their bet, and the winner gets all of it. There is no table fee between friends.\n- Each turn has 60 seconds. If you don't roll in time, you lose the duel, the same as rolling the 1.\n- If someone reloads or leaves the group before the 1, or the game hides the roll results, the duel is called off and no TapCoins move. Once the 1 has been rolled, the result stands: leaving the group or a reload then doesn't undo it.\n- Duels with friends don't work inside dungeons, raids, battlegrounds or arenas: the game hides the roll results there. Challenge each other outside.\n\n|cffffd100Casino: rock paper scissors|r\n- Pick Rock paper scissors under the top bar of the Death roll view (Death roll switches back). It plays out on a snowy mountaintop above the clouds, with little flags blowing in the wind.\n- Rock beats scissors, scissors beat paper, paper beats rock. Both cats shake a paw three times (\"rock, paper, scissors\") and then show their sign: a fist paw, an open paw, or two toes up, drawn in each cat's own fur colour. The winner hops in confetti and the loser flops over, like the death roll.\n- A small How to play box explains the rules (hover it for a tooltip too).\n\n|cffffd100Casino: rock paper scissors against the house cat|r\n- Press House cat, choose your bet and press Rock, Paper or Scissors: that places the bet. The house cat picks at random.\n- A tie plays again for free: your bet stays on the table until someone wins.\n- A win gives you 1.9 times your bet back: on a bet of 100 you win 90. Ties replay, so you win half the games, and over many games the house keeps about 5% of what is bet, the same as the death roll.\n- A game waiting after a tie waits for you, even after a reload.\n\n|cffffd100Casino: rock paper scissors with a friend|r\n- Press Friend, pick a friend in your party or raid who has TapCatForever with the arrows, choose a bet and press Challenge. They get the same small Accept or Decline box as for a death roll.\n- Best of 1, and a tie plays again. You both bet the same amount, and the winner gets the whole bet (no table fee).\n- Neither addon can see the other pick first: each one locks in its pick (it sends only a scrambled code of the pick and a random secret), and only when both are locked in do they show their picks, and each checks the other's matches what was locked in.\n- If a pick doesn't match what was locked in, or doesn't arrive within 30 seconds, the game is called off and no TapCoins move. The game says why.\n- Each pick has 60 seconds. A reload or leaving the group before the result calls the game off, and no TapCoins move.\n- Unlike death roll, it works inside dungeons and raids too: it doesn't use /roll.\n\n|cffffd100Main window|r\n- The first time you open the window on 1.6, a small What's new box over the window shows the new things in pictures. Read the full patch notes from it, or close it. The rest of the window is dimmed behind it, and closing the window closes it too. It shows once.\n- Achievements and Settings are now round buttons next to the TapCatForever title (an achievement emblem and a cog), so the other ten tabs, the Casino among them, sit in two roomier rows of five and every name fits.\n- The window can now be made bigger or smaller: drag the grip in its bottom-right corner. Everything inside grows or shrinks with it, and the top-left corner stays where it is. The size follows how far you drag, so just clicking the grip doesn't change it.\n- The window always fits on your screen: on smaller screens the largest size is a little under 140%. Double-click the grip to go back to normal size.\n- Settings > Cat and display has Window size - and + buttons too (5% a click, from 60% to 140%). The size is remembered.\n\n|cffffd100Main window: fold away the character column|r\n- A new cat button at the top, the one nearest the left column, folds away that column (your cat, gear slots, class and stats). The window gets narrower and the tabs slide left. Click it again to bring the column back. Your choice is remembered.\n- In the narrow window the Compendium is a book icon next to the layout button, and the Treasure Bag shows without its label.\n- The Casino still uses the whole window: on that tab the window grows to the left, so the tabs stay where they are, and it goes back exactly where it was when you leave, even near the edge of the screen.\n- With the column folded away, hovering an item on the Appearance, Shop, Gear or Professions page shows it on a small cat beside the window, so you can still try things on.\n- The Gear page still says to click a slot around your cat to filter: open the column with the cat button to see the slots.\n\n|cffffd100Main window: compact layout|r\n- A new layout button (a little phone, between the cat button and the Compendium button) switches the main window to a compact layout: narrow and tall, about the shape of a phone screen. Click it again (it shows a wide window then) to go back.\n- The tabs become big round buttons in two rows of five, each with its name under it and a tooltip. Quests shows how many are ready to hand in, as before. Achievements and Settings stay as the round icons by the title.\n- Every page is shown smaller to fit the narrow window and works the same as before. The Casino is shown smaller still so the whole table fits.\n- The character column has its own view: click the cat button, or the level line at the bottom, to see your cat, gear slots, class and stats. Click the cat button again, or any tab, to go back.\n- A line at the bottom shows your class, level, title, Power and XP. Your TapCoins sit next to the Treasure Bag on the second row, so big numbers have room. The Shop's round button is a chest, so it doesn't look like the Treasure Bag.\n- Trying on items works here too: a small cat beside the window shows the item while you hover it.\n- Text gets small in the compact window: drag the grip in the corner (or use Window size in Settings) to make the whole window bigger. The compact window remembers its own size, so making it bigger to read doesn't make the wide window too big.\n- Your choice is remembered. Leaving the compact window goes back to the wide window, with the character column open or folded as you left it.\n- The What's new strip over the window takes the width of the narrow and compact windows, and grows taller for its text. If the taller strip no longer fits above the window, it goes below it.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure|r\n- Auto-advance now tries the next zone 2 levels before its level (raids still wait for level 60). Travelling by hand still has no level limit.\n- The last boss of each starter zone (Elwynn Forest, Westfall, Ragefire Chasm, Wailing Caverns and The Deadmines) is a little easier: 10% extra health instead of 30%.\n- A new cat that presses about 2 keys a second now reaches Westfall after about 18 minutes of Adventure (it was about 32) and level 10 after about 31 minutes.\n- A Help button next to Bosses and loot opens \"How Adventure works\": two short pages, one on fights, stages, zones and Auto-advance, one on every reward. It also opens by itself the first time you visit the Adventure tab.\n- With Auto-advance on, a loss sends your cat back to the last trash pack; with it off, your cat drops back to an easier pack after 3 losses in a row.\n- The line under the fight now says what your cat is doing and what it waits for, for example \"Next: Wailing Caverns at level 15 (you are 14). Farming Ragefire Chasm.\"\n- The fight log and that line each have their own rows at the bottom of the page, so they never draw over each other. The log shows as many of its newest lines as fit.\n- \"Wailing Caverns opens at level 15. Running Ragefire Chasm again until then.\" is logged once, not after every run of the zone.\n- Hover the zone name to see what is left to earn there: bosses still to beat for the first time and what they give, the zone clear bonus, the chance a boss kill drops a chest right now (for example \"Cat Treat Pouch from boss kills: 12% a kill right now\"; it grows the longer your cat fights), and which bosses can drop loot again.\n- Enemies are no longer cut off by an invisible box: each one is drawn in a space that covers the whole fight scene, and is sized and placed so its attacks and its fall when it dies stay inside the fight scene's frame. The enemies stand a little further left to make room. Big bosses and wide creatures fit too, in every window size and layout.\n- Area spells (Arcane Explosion, Thunder Clap, Consecration and the others) now also go off against a single enemy, such as a boss, when no single-target spell is ready, so every class deals a little more damage to bosses. Arcane Explosion rings out from your cat before it hits every enemy.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure: enemies above your cat's level|r\n- Fights now count the level difference, like WoW. Enemies up to 3 levels above your cat fight as before.\n- For each level past that, your cat deals about 6% less damage (never under 5% of it) and takes about 6% more, and it misses more: 7% at 4 levels above and 2% more for each level after that, up to 60%. A miss shows \"Miss\" over the enemy.\n- Enemies below your cat give it a little more damage: 1% a level, at most 5%.\n- An enemy's level is the zone's lowest level for its first packs, up to 2 or 3 levels more for its last boss. Raids count as level 60.\n- When the enemies are 5 or more levels above your cat, a line in the top-left corner of the fight, above your cat, says so, for example \"Enemies here are 29 levels above your cat: it hits much less and takes far more damage.\"\n- Auto-advance's zones (2 levels early) stay winnable, and normal progression is about the same as before. A level 31 cat in Molten Core now loses within seconds. Travelling by hand still has no level limit.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure: first kills give more in bigger zones|r\n- The first time your cat beats a boss, the reward now grows with the zone:\n- Elwynn Forest and Westfall: a green piece of gear or a Cat Treat Pouch.\n- Dungeons up to level 29: a piece of the boss's loot, sometimes with a Cat Treat Pouch.\n- Dungeons from level 30: a Rare or better piece, with a chance of an Adventurer's Strongbox.\n- Dungeons from level 45: two pieces, or a piece and a Dungeon Chest.\n- Raids: two pieces with a chance of a Raider's Hoard. Final raid bosses give two or three pieces and the Hoard.\n- Final bosses keep their zone clear chest and TapCoins. TapCoins are unchanged.\n- First-kill gear is always something your cat's class can use, and never Legendary.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure: farm a boss for its loot|r\n- Bosses can now drop their real loot again after the first kill. The chance is small: at most about 0.3% a kill for a piece, most are under 0.1% a kill, and none is under 0.02%.\n- Bosses and loot (next to Help) lists each boss in the zone, its first-kill reward, and the pieces it can drop for your cat with the chance per kill.\n- Press Farm on a piece (or Farm this boss): your cat stays on that boss and fights it again and again. Auto-advance turns off while you farm and comes back when you stop.\n- The line under the fight shows \"Farming Edwin VanCleef for Cruel Barb (0.2% a kill), kills so far: 12.\"\n- Every chance is shown as a percent a kill (\"0.4% a kill\", or \"under 0.1% a kill\" for the rarest), never as a time to wait.\n- You can farm a boss you have reached but not beaten yet. Its first kill counts, and if the first-kill reward is the piece you want, farming stops there.\n- When the piece drops, farming stops with one chat line. Stop farming, moving to another stage or zone, or turning Auto-advance on also stops it at once.\n- Fighting-time chests keep their own timers while you farm.\n- Gear tooltips in the Compendium give the chance a boss drops the piece for your cat on later kills (for example \"0.2% a kill\"), and what that boss's first kill gives. The Treasure Bag's list of where chests come from now mentions first kills.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure: rewards for real WoW bosses|r\n- Some rewards now come from killing certain bosses in real World of Warcraft with TapCatForever on. Tooltips and the Compendium say \"In WoW: kill <boss> in <place>\" for these, and how many times you have killed that boss on this character.\n- Dungeon bosses count when the game says the encounter was won. They are recognised by the boss itself, so this works in every game language.\n- Hogger, out in Elwynn Forest, counts when you fought him and then see him dead (as your target, focus or nameplate). If someone else tagged him, he doesn't count.\n- Hogger: Hogger's Chewed Bandana, always on your first kill. Archmage Arugal (Shadowfang Keep): Arugal's Worgen Cowl, 20% each kill. General Drakkisath (Blackrock Spire): Drakkisath's Ember Crown, 20% each kill.\n- These skins moved from Adventure drops to the real bosses: Defias Bandit Cat (Edwin VanCleef, The Deadmines, 15%), Ragefire Cinder Cat (Taragaman the Hungerer, Ragefire Chasm, 15%) and Stone Watcher Cat (Archaedas, Uldaman, 10%). They still count for Tiger King. Adventure keeps its other boss skins, such as the Scarlet Crusader Cat and the Wind-Up Clockwork Cat.\n- Nothing needs a raid: WoW: Forever has no raids yet. All of these are Cosmetic only.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure: the window knows when you're in a dungeon|r\n- While you are inside a real dungeon, opening the TapCatForever window shows a slim banner at the bottom of the character column, in three short lines, for example \"You're in The Deadmines. / Finish it for a Dungeon Chest; 5 TapCoins a boss. / Bosses this run: 2.\"\n- It also says when this run can't give a chest (hover to see why: today's chest from this dungeon already earned, or the daily limit reached), and when the chest for this run is already in your Treasure Bag.\n- When real bosses there have rewards you don't have yet, the banner says so. Hover it to see them.\n- In a raid it says Raider's Hoard and 10 TapCoins a boss (for when WoW: Forever opens raids).\n- It updates while the window is open and is hidden outside dungeons and raids. It is part of the window, not a pop-up.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure: boss effects|r\n- Six new back effects play behind your cat. Each is unlocked by a big boss kill, in real WoW or in Adventure:\n- Storm Aura: in WoW, kill Mekgineer Thermaplugg in Gnomeregan. In Adventure, beat Ossirian the Unscarred in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj.\n- Firelord's Blaze: in WoW, kill Emperor Dagran Thaurissan in Blackrock Depths. In Adventure, beat Ragnaros in Molten Core.\n- Frostwhisper Chill: in WoW, kill Ras Frostwhisper in Scholomance. In Adventure, beat Kel'Thuzad in Naxxramas.\n- Umbral Shroud: in WoW, kill Baron Rivendare in Stratholme. In Adventure, beat Nefarian in Blackwing Lair.\n- Crusader's Radiance: in WoW, kill High Inquisitor Whitemane in Scarlet Monastery. In Adventure, beat C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj.\n- Verdant Wisps: in WoW, kill Princess Theradras in Maraudon. In Adventure, beat Hakkar in Zul'Gurub.\n- The first such kill always unlocks the effect. Wear it from Appearance like any effect. Cosmetic only.\n- Each has a look of its own: a crackling ring of lightning with storm clouds, a crown of flames, ice shards and snowflakes, curling shadow smoke, a halo with a cross of light, and a leafy vine with glowing wisps.\n- These unlocks are the one big moment that shows over your cat: \"You unlocked Storm Aura\" appears above it (over its level and XP text) with the effect playing behind it, then fades after about 5 seconds. Two unlocks at once show one after the other. Nothing else pops up. The \"Popups on cat\" setting turns it off.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure: fight visuals|r\n- Hunters with a bow, gun, crossbow or thrown weapon now shoot it: arrows, bullets (with a muzzle flash), bolts and spinning throwing knives fly from the weapon your cat holds to the enemy. The damage number shows when the shot lands, and a killing shot lands before the enemy falls.\n- Mages, priests and warlocks with a wand equipped shoot wand bolts between their spells. The bolt takes the colour of the wand's damage (fire, frost, shadow, arcane, holy or nature) and lands with the game's own spell effect of that school.\n- Casters without a wand cast a small spell instead. Warriors, rogues and paladins keep their melee swings, now with a small swipe on the enemy. A druid in Cat Form swipes too.\n- While it is out fighting, a cat that shoots holds its bow, gun or wand in its paw, also between packs. A cosmetic weapon stays in its paw only when it is the same kind (a cosmetic bow for a bow or crossbow, a rifle for a gun, a wand for a wand).\n- A hunter with nothing in its ranged slot fights in melee (it used to get a pretend ranged weapon). Hunters still get their starter bow. For such a hunter the Power number used by expeditions and the leaderboard is a little lower than before.\n- Abilities that hit enemies now play the game's real spell effects on the enemy models (Fireball's explosion, Corruption's shadow while it lasts, Frost Nova's ice while enemies are frozen, and so on), on top of the cartoon effects. Single-target spells play only on that enemy; area spells play on every enemy.\n- A lasting effect stays on when other spells or wand bolts hit the same enemy. When two lasting effects meet (Corruption, then Fear), the newer one shows and the other comes back when it ends.\n- Stunned, frozen, rooted or feared enemies stand dazed for as long as it lasts. Other enemies flinch when an ability hits them.\n- Passive abilities show too: auras (Devotion Aura, Trueshot Aura, Inner Fire, Shadowform, Frost Armor, Blessing of Might) glow at the cat's feet when a pack appears, Seal of Righteousness sparkles with every hit, the hunter's pet claws at the enemy, the Searing Totem stands by the cat and throws fire, Lightning Shield orbs circle the cat, the Voidwalker's shield flashes when the cat is hit, and Cat Form sparkles.\n- Buffs, heals and shields on the cat stay cartoon effects.\n\n|cffffd100Professions|r\n- Skill-ups work like WoW: the first few crafts or clicks on something new always give a skill point. After that it slows down a lot, and once your skill is 50 above it, it teaches you nothing more. Move on to the next spot or recipe to keep learning.\n- Recipes, gathering spots, seeds, bandages, fishing spots and dishes are coloured like in WoW: orange always teaches you, yellow often, green sometimes, pale green rarely, grey no longer. Hover one to see \"Still teaches you: often\" (or sometimes, rarely, no longer).\n- Gathering spots count too: your first spot teaches up to 50, the second up to 100, and so on.\n- Recipe materials were lowered so levelling a craft to 300 still takes about six weeks of normal play.\n- Some miners swear their veins act strangely at sixteen past the hour.\n\n|cffffd100Professions: white starter sets|r\n- Blacksmithing, Leatherworking and Tailoring can each make a cheap white starter set at low skill, so a new cat can wear a full crafted set.\n- Blacksmithing: Copper Bracers, Copper Chain Pants, Rough Copper Vest, Light Chain Gloves, Copper Chain Boots, Copper Chain Belt and a copper weapon (mace, axe, shortsword or claymore).\n- Leatherworking: Handstitched Leather Bracers, Boots, Vest, Cloak, Pants and Belt, and Rough Leather Gloves.\n- Tailoring: Linen Cloak, Simple Linen Pants, Knitted Gloves, Brown Linen Vest, Knitted Bracers, Linen Belt and Simple Linen Boots.\n- Each piece costs about 5 to 9 of your first material.\n- While your crafting skill is under 75 the set is shown first on the Crafting page, with \"Starter set 3/7 made\" at the top. Pieces you made, have in your bag or wear count.\n- All the higher crafted gear is still there.\n\n|cffffd100Professions: more spots|r\n- Every gathering profession has three more spots, after the first six. They open up as your business grows and stay open once you have them:\n- Mining: Dark Iron Deposit (Blackrock Depths) at Renown 100, Elementium Vein (Blackwing Lair) at Renown 500 and Mining 250, Obsidian Chunk (Ahn'Qiraj) at 1Qa Trade Gold earned in total and Mining 300.\n- Skinning: Zul'Gurub Bats (Primal Bat Leather), Molten Core Hounds (Core Leather) and Silithid Swarm in Ahn'Qiraj (Heavy Silithid Carapace), opening the same way.\n- Tailoring: Moonwell in Felwood (Mooncloth), Ironweb Spiders in Blackrock Spire (Ironweb Spider Silk) and the Cult of the Damned in Naxxramas (Wartorn Cloth Scrap).\n- Renown here means the highest Renown your cat has ever had. Skill means your gathering skill, which you raise by working spots by hand.\n- They cost more and earn more than the first six, with their own helpers and profit upgrades. Selling the business resets them like the other spots.\n- Scroll the spots with the mouse wheel or the arrows under them.\n- Their materials are not used in any recipe yet. The spot's tooltip says so.\n\n|cffffd100Professions: crafted cosmetics cost more|r\n- Cosmetic only recipes (fur colours and the other cosmetics in every profession) now need a lot more of the materials they are made from: 5 times as much for uncommon ones, 10 times for rare ones, 20 times for epic and 40 times for legendary ones. Fur colours cost 10 times or more, by rarity.\n- Rare ingredients stay as they were: Black Lotus, Mr. Pinchy, bandages, dishes and bought spices.\n- Gear recipes cost the same as before.\n\n|cffffd100Loot and chests|r\n- Chests now belong to the class cat that earned them. Each cat has its own Treasure Bag.\n- Chests earned while you play a class go to that cat. Level-up chests go to the cat that levelled, even when expedition XP levelled it while you played another cat.\n- Professions helpers and fishing buddies put their chests in their own cat's bag.\n- Expedition chests go to a cat that went: the cat you are playing if it was in the party, otherwise the party's first cat. Any other chest you earn while claiming (a level-up, an achievement) still goes to its own cat.\n- Bought chests are for the cat you are playing.\n- Chests you already had move once to the cat you are playing when you log in, stamped with its level.\n- Every chest is stamped with the level of the cat that earned it (\"Lv 20\"). A chest holds gear for its level, even if you open it much later: a level 20 chest opened at level 40 still holds level 20 gear.\n- Gear is never more than 3 levels above the chest's level. When there is nothing of the rolled quality near that level, you get the next quality down instead.\n- Raid gear only comes from chests of level 55 and up. A real Legendary only from level 60 chests.\n- The opening reel shows gear for the chest's level.\n\n|cffffd100Loot and chests: the Treasure Bag|r\n- One row per kind of chest and level, for example \"Lv 20\". How many you have is on the chest's icon. The level turns grey once your cat is well past it.\n- Five rows a page, with page buttons (or the mouse wheel) when there are more.\n- Hover a row for \"Holds gear for about level 20\", that chest's odds and where that kind of chest comes from.\n- Open opens one chest of that row's level. If that level is already used up, it opens nothing. All opens every chest of that kind. Open everything empties this cat's bag.\n- The title says whose bag it is, and a line lists chests waiting in your other cats' bags.\n\n|cffffd100Loot and chests: a care package for players who were already playing|r\n- The first time a character that played before this update logs in, every one of your cats that has been played gets a plain white piece for each empty gear slot it can use at its level, once per cat.\n- The pieces go into that cat's gear bag. Nothing is equipped for you.\n- Once per account there are also 150 TapCoins.\n- One chat line says what you got. No pop-up, and it never comes twice.\n- Brand-new characters and accounts don't get one.\n\n|cffffd100Gear|r\n- The Usable only box on the Gear page now also hides gear above your cat's level, so it only lists what your cat can put on now.\n- 171 real Classic item sets are in the game, from Defias Leather and Embrace of the Viper to Battlegear of Valor, Zul'Gurub, Ahn'Qiraj and tier 1 to 3, plus crafted sets like Devilsaur, Volcanic and Bloodvine.\n- Wear enough pieces of a set and its set bonuses count: they add to Power, Adventure and expeditions, and Equip best and every upgrade check include them.\n- Bonuses a cat can't use (procs, class spell changes, resistances, defense, dodge, block value, mana per 5 sec) are shown in grey with \"(no effect on your cat)\". They never count as an active bonus.\n- The gear tooltip shows the set: its name with how many pieces your cat wears, every piece (worn in white, the rest in grey) and the bonuses (active in green, not yet in grey). On a party member's cat it counts the pieces that cat wears.\n- Comparing gear now also says when a swap gains or loses a set bonus.\n- The Compendium has a new Item Sets list: every set with how many pieces you have, a class filter, and Owned for complete sets. Hover a set for its pieces and bonuses.\n- Real shoulder gear now shows on your cat as pauldrons on both shoulders, in the colours of the item: plate, mail, leather and cloth each have their own shape.\n- Every real shoulder look in the game has its own cartoon drawing, made from the item's icon (43 in all): gold domes over mail, tall red fins, quilted leather, shaggy mantles with orbs, the tauren skull, the glowing Netherwind runes, Ten Storms lightning and more.\n- Pauldrons sit over capes and chest pieces and under hoods and big helms, and your paws stay in front of them. Party members see your shoulders too.\n\n|cffffd100Party expeditions|r\n- In a party or raid with friends who have TapCatForever, open Expeditions and pick Party (top right).\n- Choose your cats (up to 3; with none picked your current cat goes), a dungeon or raid, a length (15 min, 30 min, 1 h, 2 h or 4 h) and a difficulty (Normal, Hard or Heroic), then press Invite my group.\n- Your friends get a small invite just above their cat: \"<Name> invites your cat: <place>, 30 min, Hard\" with Accept and Decline. It goes away after 60 seconds, which counts as a no. In combat it shrinks to a smaller box with the same buttons, so it never runs out unseen. It is also shown in the Party view, where you can pick more cats before you accept.\n- It sets off as soon as everyone has answered, or after 60 seconds with at least one player. The one who invited can also press Start now, or Call off. Up to 5 players go.\n- If your group can't get addon messages for a while (in combat in an instance, for example), it sets off as soon as they can, up to a few minutes later. Nobody ends up on an expedition the others don't know about.\n- Everyone's cats add up their Power. A harder difficulty and more players need more Power. The Party view shows what each place needs and what it gives.\n- Once it has set off it keeps going for everyone, even if the group breaks up or someone logs out. Everyone gets the same result.\n- Each player claims their own rewards with Claim: XP for each cat that went, a few TapCoins, chest rolls (one per hour away, part of one for shorter trips; one more with 3 or more players) and +10% XP and TapCoins for every other player. Heroic also has a small chance of a Dungeon Chest or a Raider's Hoard. A failure brings half the XP and a few TapCoins.\n- Party expeditions have their own slot: your two solo expedition slots stay free. A cat on a party expedition can't go on a solo one (or into Adventure) until it is back.\n- One invite at a time. Party members need the newest TapCatForever to join. Members on an older version don't hold the invite up.\n\n|cffffd100Party cats|r\n- Your own cat no longer shows up in the small row of party cats: the addon now learns the name the game gives you from your own messages, also when it can't read your name directly. Only your friends' cats sit there, also right after a reload.\n\n|cffffd100Achievements|r\n- The Achievements tab has two views: Account (the achievements you know, shared by every character) and This class.\n- In This class, every class's cat has its own 23 achievements: levels 10 to 60, Elwynn Forest and Westfall, Adventure dungeons and raids cleared, every ability learned, a full Rare set and a full Epic set worn, crafting skill 150 and 300, five crafted pieces worn at once, expeditions finished and party expeditions finished.\n- Pick a class with the class icons at the bottom of the page to see its progress. Hover a row for the details.\n- Each class earns each one once for your whole account, so an alt of the same class can't earn it again.\n- Rewards are a few TapCoins (595 for all 23 of one class) and a chest for that class's cat, which goes straight into that cat's own Treasure Bag.\n- Level 60 with a class also gives that class's cat its Legendary main hand look. It is labelled Cosmetic only: it changes how your cat looks, not its Power.\n- Already played a lot? At login your cats get credit for what they have already done, with one chat line.\n- Expeditions count for every cat that went, from this update on. Party expeditions count for Better Together and Party Regular, and as expeditions for the expedition ones.\n- Natural: get a blackjack (25 TapCoins).\n- Three Cats in a Row: line up three cats on the slots (100 TapCoins).\n\n|cffffd100Cosmetics and art|r\n- Each class's cat now has its own look and its own collection: skins, furs, patterns, tap effects, hats, capes, effects, accessories, racial pieces, set pieces and crafted cosmetics. Switch class and that cat puts on its own look and shows its own collection.\n- After the update every class's cat owns everything your characters owned and starts with the look it was wearing, so nobody loses anything. A brand-new cat starts in its own class fur.\n- From now on a new cosmetic goes to the cat you are playing: chests, Adventure drops, real WoW boss rewards, quests, achievements and the Shop (skins and the racial piece too). Crafting, an expedition and a class achievement give it to the cat that earned it.\n- A cosmetic a cat already has is salvaged for TapCoins, as before. The same cosmetic on another cat is new for that cat.\n- The Appearance tab, the Shop (what you own, and the skins a Heroic Cache can still hold), the Compendium, trying on and \"Got it from\" all show the cat you are playing.\n- Achievements that count cosmetics (Wardrobe Started to Completionist, Crazy Cat Collector and the others) count your best cat's collection, so playing another cat never loses progress.\n- Party members, the Casino, the Shop's try on and the Gear page show the look of the cat you are playing.\n- Cosmetics can now move on your cat: flickering flames, lava that flows, glows that breathe, stars drifting inside a helm or through the fur, rising embers, falling snow and leaves, bubbles, sparkles and ghostly wisps.\n- Effects only play on the cartoon cat and stop while the cat is hidden. Small cats (the party row) show only the light parts, and they come back when you make the cat bigger.\n- Don't want them? Untick \"Animated cosmetics\" at the top of the Appearance tab for still pictures. You keep everything either way.\n- Every Epic and Legendary cat skin now has its own animated effect. Diamond Cat sparkles with glints and a shine that sweeps across its fur. Galaxy Cat has stars and soft nebula clouds drifting inside its fur. Spectral Tiger glows and trails ghostly wisps. Golden Treasure Cat shimmers with a gold shine and glints.\n- Fire cats (Primal Flamesaber, Emberheart, Onyxian Whelpling, Ragefire Cinder, Vermillion Lynx) give off embers, and Primal Flamesaber has fire moving in its fur. Frost cats (Winterspring Frostsaber, Mr. Bigglesworth) have falling snow and frost glints. Shadow cats (Shadow Dusk Dreamsaber, Swift Zulian Panther, Skeletal Cat) trail wisps; Rainbow Cat's markings shift colour; Runebound Cat's runes pulse.\n- Legendary cosmetic pieces shine: a light sweeps across them now and then. Epic helms, chest pieces and shoulders catch a couple of small glints now and then. Frozen Throne Crown, Crown of the Tapmaster, Wings of the Eternal Tapper, Felcloth Wings and Black Lotus have their own sparkles, snow or embers. The Spectral and Starlight furs glow and twinkle.\n\n|cffffd100Cosmetics and art: dungeon sets|r\n- Eleven animated cosmetic sets, one for Molten Core and one for each later dungeon in Adventure, six pieces each: a helm or crown, shoulders, chest, cape, weapon and aura. Cosmetic only.\n- Each piece always drops from one boss of that dungeon or raid in Adventure until you own it. The final boss gives the helm. The Compendium and tooltips show the set's progress, such as \"Dire Maul set (2/6)\", and which boss drops each piece.\n- Molten Core: Crown of the Firelord (crown with flickering flames, Ragnaros), Golemagg's Molten Pauldrons (Golemagg the Incinerator), Lava-Heart Breastplate (lava flows through its seams, Garr), Magmadar's Cinder Drape (a cape with burning edges, Magmadar), Lucifron's Firehammer (Lucifron) and Baron Geddon's Ember Aura (a heat glow and rising embers, Baron Geddon).\n- Scarlet Monastery: crimson and gold with holy light, a winged helm under a halo, and feathers drifting down.\n- Uldaman: titan stone with glowing blue runes and violet crystals, with shards floating around the crown and staff.\n- Zul'Farrak: a striped sun headdress with a blazing sun turning behind it, a scarab collar, and a sandstorm.\n- Maraudon: living wood with antlers, violet blossoms, falling leaves and fireflies.\n- Sunken Temple: a serpent hood with a frill of swirling water, jade scales, a trident and rising bubbles.\n- Blackrock Depths: Dark Iron forge armour with turning gears, furnace fire, sparks and smoke.\n- Blackrock Spire: a storm dragon helm with wings, with lightning crackling over every piece.\n- Dire Maul: moonsilver and a night sky full of drifting stars, with planets circling the crown and staff.\n- Scholomance: bone and green soulfire, a skull crown, a ribcage of swirling souls and a reaper's scythe.\n- Stratholme: runed steel and living ice, with huge ice horns and falling snow.\n\n|cffffd100Cosmetics and art: shoulders and the racial slot|r\n- The cat has a new Shoulders slot in the Appearance tab. Shoulder cosmetics come from the dungeon sets, so it stays empty until your cat earns its first set shoulders.\n- The racial heritage accessory (tusks, horns, ears, beard, goggles, feathers...) now has its own slot, so you can wear it together with sunglasses, a monocle, a bow tie or any other accessory.\n- Face accessories sit on top of it (shades over tusks), neck accessories under it (a dwarf beard over a bow tie).\n- The Appearance tab and the Compendium call it the Racial slot. \"Show racial accessory\" in Settings still hides or shows it.\n- If you wore it in the accessory slot before, it moves to the new slot on its own.\n- Party members on this version see both; older versions see the accessory only.\n\n|cffffd100Cosmetics and art: where every cosmetic came from|r\n- Skins, effects, tap effects and other cosmetics now remember where you got them. Hover one in the Appearance tab or the Compendium: \"Got it from: Heroic Cache, 3 days ago\".\n- When you got another copy later, a second line says where the latest one came from.\n- Sources include chests, Adventure bosses, real dungeon runs, expeditions, quests, achievements, crafting, the Shop and the Appearance tab.\n- Cosmetics you had before this update say \"Got before this was tracked\". Another copy of one later adds \"Latest one from: ...\" under it.\n- The cosmetics every cat starts with say \"Got it from: Starter cosmetic\".\n\n|cffffd100Skins|r\n- The three best-looking cat skins now come from the hardest bosses. If you already have one, you keep it.\n- Galaxy Cat: no longer in the Shop. In Adventure, Kel'Thuzad in Naxxramas drops it, 2% each kill.\n- Diamond Cat: no longer in the Heroic Cache. In WoW, kill General Drakkisath in Blackrock Spire with TapCatForever on, 5% each kill. In Adventure, Nefarian in Blackwing Lair drops it, 2% each kill.\n- Emberheart Cat: in Adventure, Ragnaros in Molten Core drops it, 3% each kill. The Molten Core expedition still has a 1% chance (it was 2%).\n- Shop skins with an animated effect cost more: Golden War Lion 12,000 TapCoins (the Spectral Tiger stays 12,000), Arcanist's Manasaber 8,000, Felsaber and Winterspring Frostsaber 7,000, Vermillion Lynx 6,500 and X-995 Mechanocat 6,000.\n- The plain Shop skins cost a little more too: Strawberry Sweetheart, Darkmoon Kitty and Maine Coon 2,500, Bengal and Spotted Frostsaber 2,000, Calico, Striped Frostsaber, Striped Nightsaber and Black Nightsaber 1,800, and the others 300 to 800.\n- Skins you already bought stay yours.\n\n|cffffd100Quests|r\n- Tap quests ask for a lot more: the daily Paws of Fury is now 4,000, 8,000 or 12,000 taps, and the weekly Tireless Tapper is 100,000 taps (it gives a little more too). New quests use the new numbers from the next daily and weekly reset.\n\n|cffffd100Realm leaderboard|r\n- Players in your party, raid or guild who joined now show up on each other's board: your summary goes out under the name the game gives you, and never under a stand-in name while that name isn't known yet.\n- Rows named \"You\" (or \"Unknown\") that older versions shared when they couldn't read a player's name are taken off every board.\n- A short note on the Leaderboard tab says it is still being worked on: other players may not show up for you yet." },
  { version = "1.5.3.6", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Realm leaderboard|r\n- Players in the same party, raid or guild now show up on each other's leaderboard on clients where the game doesn't give addons the realm's name. Before, the leaderboard had nowhere to keep other players, so only your own row showed.\n- /tcf lbdebug prints what the leaderboard sees (where it sends, how many messages it heard and kept). Send it to the developer if players still don't show up.\n\n|cffffd100Party cats|r\n- Your own cat no longer shows up in the little row beside your cat, however the game writes your realm. Only your party members' cats are there.\n- The row no longer blinks when someone changes their gear: a cat only leaves the row when that player is really gone from the group.\n- Click a party member's cat to see its profile: the cat drawn big, its class and level, and the gear it wears (hover a piece for its details)." },
  { version = "1.5.3.5", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Gear|r\n- Gear your cat is wearing no longer shows in the Gear page's list. It is on the slots around your cat; right-click a slot to take the piece off and it goes back into the list. A spare copy of something you wear still shows, marked Also worn." },
  { version = "1.5.3.4", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Professions|r\n- The later professions now need much more Trade Gold earned in total: Herbalism 1B, First Aid 50T, Fishing 1Qa and Cooking 50Qa (before: 25M, 2.5B, 250B and 2T). Trade Gold grows fast, so the old amounts came far too soon. Now you need a few rounds of selling your business for Renown, which makes your gold come faster, to reach them.\n- Professions you already learned stay learned.\n- Renown alone no longer unlocks a profession; only Trade Gold earned does.\n\n|cffffd100Chests|r\n- A chest you open while the reel is still spinning now gets its own spin right after, instead of skipping it." },
  { version = "1.5.3.3", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Chests|r\n- Every chest you open shows the loot box with your item when the reel ends again, whatever its quality.\n\n|cffffd100Realm leaderboard|r\n- Your own cat always shows on the leaderboard once you joined, also on realms whose names have dots, brackets or other characters the leaderboard didn't expect. Players on those realms can now share with each other too.\n- If something goes wrong while the leaderboard draws, it now says so on the tab (and once in chat) instead of showing an empty board." },
  { version = "1.5.3.2", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Realm leaderboard|r\n- The leaderboard now shares through your party, raid and guild, the same way party cats work. Group up or be in a guild with friends who joined and you see each other right away, and they pass on the players they know, so the board grows as you play together.\n- When someone joins your group, your cat is shared with them within a few seconds.\n- WoW: Forever doesn't seem to allow addon messages on custom channels, which the leaderboard relied on until now, so players often didn't show up. It still tries that channel where the game allows it." },
  { version = "1.5.3.1", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Chests|r\n- Chests now give gear for your cat's level: never more than 3 levels above it. Before, a chest could reach about 20 levels too high when it couldn't find gear of the rolled quality near your level.\n- When there is no gear of the rolled quality near your level, you get the next quality down instead of gear you can't wear yet.\n- Epics from chests are dungeon and raid boss loot only. Rare open-world Epics like Staff of Jordan no longer come from chests, and a chest never gives you a second copy of an Epic you already have.\n- Raid boss Epics (from the Raider's Hoard and the rarest chest rolls) are level 60 gear, so they come only to cats of level 55 and up. Younger cats get the best gear near their level instead. Real legendaries only drop for level 60 cats.\n- A chest prefers gear your cat doesn't have yet.\n- The odds shown on each chest and the items on its reel now match what it can really give your cat.\n- Gear you already got stays yours.\n\n|cffffd100Opening chests|r\n- Every chest you open yourself spins the reel again, pouches included. The loot box after it only shows for blue or better; for a green or white the reel lands and a slim line shows what you got." },
  { version = "1.5.3", highlight = "New: a realm leaderboard tab. Join it to see other players' taps and get a big chest for your level. Also level 60, faster unlocks and more.", text = "|cffffd100Realm leaderboard|r\n- New: a Leaderboard tab in the main window, with the cats of players on your realm. Open it with the tab, the Leaderboard button in Settings > Help and info, /tcf top or /tcf leaderboard. The tabs are now two rows of six to make room for it.\n- It has three sections. Total taps ranks everyone by total taps, and you can sort by cat level, achievements earned or Adventure zones cleared instead. Per class has a button for each of the nine classes and ranks players' cats of that class by cat level, with ties going to more taps. Professions ranks Trade Gold earned by all of a player's cats, and the best Blacksmithing, Leatherworking, Tailoring, Herbalism, First Aid, Fishing and Cooking skill of any of their cats. Your own row is highlighted in every section.\n- It is opt-in and off by default. Until you join, the tab shows what the leaderboard is, exactly what is shared and with whom, and a Join the leaderboard button. Joining turns on Share my cat's progress (developer stats and leaderboard) in Settings > Help and info, the same option as the developer stats, which you can also use there. A Leave button on the tab turns it off again after a short question. Only players who joined are on the leaderboard and can see it.\n- The first time you join, the character you are playing gets a Heroic Cache in its Treasure Bag, with one chat line. This happens once for your account: leaving and joining again, or joining on another character, gives nothing more.\n- When it is on, your addon sends your character's name and realm, your cat's class and level, the level of each of your class cats, your total taps, achievements earned, Adventure zones cleared, Trade Gold earned, your best profession skills and addon version on an addon channel that TapCatForever players on your realm join when they turn it on. Players pass the list on to each other inside the game, so you also see players you are never online with. Nothing goes over the internet, and the channel never shows in your chat. Anyone who joins that channel could read what is shared there with an addon.\n- The option is for your whole account, so all your characters share. Since taps and achievements are shared between them, other players may be able to tell your characters on the same realm belong together.\n- The leaderboard fills up over time and can be a little behind. Players not seen for 30 days drop off, and up to 500 players are kept. Turning the option off stops sharing and asks other players to take you off their leaderboard. Players who are offline then hear it later from the others, and each of your other characters that shared asks the next time you log in on it.\n- One player can only add a limited number of other players to your leaderboard each hour, and a player who took themselves off only comes back by sharing again.\n- Your taps are shared about every 2 minutes while you play, so the board stays current.\n\n|cffffd100Levels|r\n- Cat levels now stop at 60, like Classic. A cat above 60 becomes 60 and keeps its gear, abilities and titles. A cat at 60 no longer gains XP, and its XP bar says Max level.\n- Early levels are faster than before: up to about level 30 each level needs less XP. After about 30 each level takes longer than before, up to about twice as long near 60. Playing about 2 hours a day, a new cat reaches level 10 in about an hour and level 60 in a few months.\n- Your cats keep the same share of their current level when the new XP amounts come in, so no cat skips levels or loses its progress toward the next one.\n- The last two level titles and achievements moved to levels you can reach: Legendary Lap Cat at level 55 and Eternal Tapper at level 60. Achievements you already have are kept.\n- The Growing Up daily quest is no longer offered when all your cats are level 60.\n- Level-up TapCoins and level chests are now paid once per class and level for your whole account. A new character, or one you reset, gets them again only above the highest level your account already reached with that class. Reset this character says so before you confirm.\n\n|cffffd100Dungeon Chest|r\n- New chest: the Dungeon Chest. It always holds gear: boss loot from the Adventure dungeons your cat has reached (Ragefire Chasm if it has reached none), close to your cat's level. Mostly Rare, some Uncommon, a little Epic, never Legendary. When those dungeons have nothing of that quality near your cat's level, it gives gear of that quality from around the world at your cat's level instead.\n- The first clear of each dungeon in Adventure gives a Dungeon Chest instead of an Adventurer's Strongbox. After that, finishing a dungeon again gives one about every 2 to 3 hours of dungeon fighting. Open-world zones still give a Strongbox for the first clear.\n- Finishing a real WoW dungeon now always gives a Dungeon Chest, instead of a Cat Treat Pouch, Adventurer's Strongbox or Heroic Cache picked by your level. The limits are the same: once a day for each dungeon, and up to 2 a day across your characters.\n- The Golden Treasure Cat and Diamond Cat can still turn up after a real WoW dungeon, at the same odds as when dungeons sometimes gave a Heroic Cache.\n- The Deadmines, Scarlet Monastery, Blackrock Depths and Stratholme expeditions sometimes bring home a Dungeon Chest (2%, 5%, 10% and 15% when they succeed).\n- The Dungeon Chest is not sold in the Shop. The Treasure Bag has a row for it.\n- New achievements: Spoils of the Deep and Dungeon Crawler (open 1 and 25 Dungeon Chests).\n\n|cffffd100Loot|r\n- Chests now and then hold a few TapCoins on top of their contents. Most hold none, about a third hold a few (2 to 15, by chest) and about 1 in 20 holds a bigger handful (40 to 300, by chest). The loot box shows them as one plain line, such as +12 TapCoins, and a small find from a chest shows them on its slim line.\n- Small finds now go to your cat's weapon (a ranged weapon for Hunters) and the gear you can see (head, chest, belt, cloak, neck, rings and off-hand) well ahead of hands, feet, wrists, legs and shoulders.\n- Burning Crusade and later items no longer drop anywhere, including Outland quest greens, Gnomish goggles, Jewelcrafting rings and blood elf and draenei starting gear. You keep any you already have.\n- Uncommon or better items with no stats at all, such as on-use trinkets like Talisman of Arathor, no longer drop. They did nothing for your cat. You keep any you already have.\n- Leftover test items that older versions let drop, such as Warbranch of Cenarius (a blue staff at item level 1 with no stats), no longer drop. Any your cats had are taken off them once, and you get their sell value in TapCoins. A cat left without a weapon gets its class weapon back.\n\n|cffffd100Gear and looks|r\n- Every class starts with a weapon of its own: a sword for Warriors, a mace for Paladins, a bow for Hunters, a dagger for Rogues and Warlocks, an axe for Shamans, and a different staff each for Priests, Mages and Druids.\n- A cat can always wear its class's starter weapon, whatever the weapon's level. A cat still holding the weapon an older version gave it gets the new one, unless that would push out an off-hand item you chose or lower its Power. Then the new one waits in its bag. Hunters keep their bow, and a weapon you picked yourself is left alone.\n- Capes and cloaks now hang down both sides of your cat and tuck in behind it, with no band across the bottom under the paws. Cosmetic capes use the same shape.\n- An Equip best button on the Gear page puts on the gear in your bag that gives your cat the most Power.\n\n|cffffd100Professions|r\n- Herbalism, First Aid, Fishing and Cooking now unlock as each cat earns Trade Gold: 25M, 2.5B, 250B and 2T earned in total. Selling your business for Renown never lowers this, and Renown makes the gold come faster. The old Renown amounts still unlock them too, and professions you already unlocked stay unlocked.\n- When a cat can learn a new profession you get one chat line, once. A cat you aren't playing hears about it the next time you play it.\n- The Professions page shows how much Trade Gold a locked profession needs and how far along this cat is, for example So far: 5.00M (20%).\n- Crafting: an All button next to Craft makes a recipe as many times as your materials allow (up to 50).\n\n|cffffd100Adventure|r\n- Enemies are measured and sized to fit the fight scene, so big ones such as the Foe Reaper 4000 are no longer cut off, and every enemy stands on the ground.\n\n|cffffd100Settings|r\n- The Settings page is sorted into clear groups: Cat and display, Chat and sounds, Position, Help and info, and Progress.\n- A new Text distance slider sets the space between the cat and its level, XP bar and counters. It works with the text above or below the cat, and the cat stays where it is.\n- A new option, Share my cat's progress (developer stats and leaderboard), is off by default. When it is on and the developer asks, your addon answers with five things: the addon version, your cat's class, cat level, zones cleared and TapCoins. It only answers the developer, only while you are both online, and nothing from it prints in your chat. The same option puts you on the realm leaderboard (see above). To share, your addon joins an addon channel, which the game still lists in its Chat Channels window.\n- Help and info has the Welcome tour, Patch notes, Send feedback and a new Compendium button side by side, with the sharing option and the Leaderboard button under them.\n- The minimap button says whether it will show or hide the icon.\n- The two reset buttons sit on their own at the bottom, in red, so they are hard to click by accident. Both still ask first.\n- Scroll the mouse wheel over a slider to move it one step at a time. The Ctrl and Shift mouse wheel tips for the cat are now in the Cat size and Opacity slider tooltips.\n\n|cffffd100Other fixes|r\n- WoW: Forever has no raids yet, so nothing needs a real raid: the Raid Leader Cat now comes from finishing any real dungeon (2%, raids too once they open), and the Raid Cat achievement counts raid zones cleared in Adventure.\n- Every \"how to get it\" line now says where: \"Adventure:\" for the Adventure game, \"In WoW:\" for real World of Warcraft.\n- Party cats: your own cat no longer shows up in the little row beside your cat.\n- Messages, notices and achievement names use plainer wording, without exclamation marks.\n- Up to 10 taps every second earn TapCoins, however fast you tap. Faster taps still count as taps and XP." },
  { version = "1.5.2", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100Quieter loot|r\n- Nothing pops up over your cat anymore. Gear and cosmetics you find while playing (lucky finds from tapping, Adventure drops, quests, expeditions) go straight into your bags without a notice box.\n- With the TapCatForever window open, gear you find shows as one slim line under the window that fades after a few seconds. Hover it to compare it with what your cat wears; click it to open the Gear tab.\n- Opening a chest plays the reel and shows the loot box only for a blue (Rare) or better item. A common or green item from a chest gets the same slim line instead.\n- Earning a chest, clearing a zone and an expedition coming back no longer show a note over the cat.\n\n|cffffd100Fixes|r\n- Hunters always have a bow: a hunter cat without a ranged weapon gets its bow, and the cat holds it." },
  { version = "1.5.1", highlight = "Each class's cat now has its own Trade Gold and Renown, real legendaries can drop, raids give the new Raider's Hoard, and there is lots more gear.", text = "|cffffd100Each class has its own professions|r\n- Every class's cat now has its own Trade Gold, Renown, gathering spots, tool, helpers, upgrades, skills and materials, and its own Herbalism garden, First Aid, Fishing and Cooking. Before, all the cats on a character shared one pile of Trade Gold.\n- Switch class and the Professions tab shows that cat's own business. The tab says whose gold you are looking at.\n- The cats you aren't playing keep working: their foremen, trappers, scavengers, gardener, field medic, fishing buddy and sous-chef run online and offline (up to 24 hours), and what they earn goes to that cat. They do it quietly, without chat lines or loot pop-ups.\n- Each cat earns its own milestone chests and sells its own business for its own Renown.\n- A Well Fed buff helps the cat that ate the dish.\n- Achievements count the Trade Gold of all your cats together, and the best Renown of one cat.\n\n|cffffd100Your progress moves over on its own|r\n- On your first login, everything your character had goes to the cat you are playing: its Trade Gold, Renown, unlocked professions, garden, bandages, fish, dishes and materials.\n- If you had also built up another main profession by switching class (for example Mining on a Warrior while you play a Mage), those spots, its tool, upgrades, milestones, skills and materials go to the cat of that profession you played most. That cat starts with no Trade Gold or Renown of its own.\n- If the cat you are playing has First Aid, it keeps the cloth that First Aid uses.\n- Your other cats start fresh, at Renown 0. Each one learns Herbalism, First Aid, Fishing and Cooking with its own Renown, and its helpers earn without the Renown bonus of the cat you are playing.\n- Your Trade Gold, spots, materials and items are not lost or doubled, and milestone chests you already got are not paid again.\n- Speed boosts and spot prices now count only each cat's own spots. If you had spots in two professions, each cat's next spots cost less, but speed boosts that came from adding both together are worked out again from that cat's own spots.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure|r\n- Clearing a zone for the first time now pays a few hundred TapCoins on top of the chest: 200 for Elwynn Forest, 50 more for each zone after it (1,550 for Naxxramas). The first of your cats to clear a zone gets the full amount; another class clearing it later gets a quarter.\n\n|cffffd100Gear|r\n- Hovering a piece of gear shows the item your cat is wearing in that slot right beside it, like WoW's own comparison, along with the Power change.\n\n|cffffd100Loot|r\n- New chest: the Raider's Hoard. It always holds gear: Epic boss loot from the raids your cat has reached (the first raid if it has reached none). Raid bosses in Adventure drop one about every 3 hours of fighting, the first clear of a raid zone gives one, real WoW raids give one (once a week each), and the Molten Core, Blackwing Lair and Naxxramas expeditions sometimes bring one home. It is never sold in the Shop, and the Treasure Bag has a new row for it.\n- Real Legendary gear can now drop, picked for your class: about 1 in 500 Heroic Caches and 1 in 100 Raider's Hoards hold one. Before, a Legendary roll gave a raid boss Epic.\n- The Cat Treat Pouch, the smallest chest, keeps its small chance of a Rare (blue) piece: about 1 in 12 pouches. It now gives one at every level. Before, at levels with no blue gear close by, it quietly gave a green instead.\n- Much more world gear for every class: about 750 white (Common) pieces with plain armor or damage, and about 1,600 Classic green items that drop with random bonuses such as \"of the Monkey\", \"of the Bear\" or \"of the Owl\" (about 4,900 versions in all).\n- Small finds: trash enemies in Adventure now and then drop a white or green piece for your level. They favour slots your cat has empty, then upgrades, so a new cat fills most of its slots in its first hour or so. Finds slow down as your slots fill and as your cat finds more, so chests and bosses stay the main source of good loot.\n- White gear is never in chests. Sell junk and the Gear page handle it like other gear.\n\n|cffffd100Professions help|r\n- Each profession now explains itself: the first time you open one, a short \"How it works\" guide shows how gathering, crafting real gear with stats or cosmetic-only items, upgrades and Renown work, and where crafted items go. The Help button next to the profession's name opens it again.\n\n|cffffd100Other fixes|r\n- The welcome tour now always reaches new players, even if something else went wrong while logging in.\n- Prices and sources on item squares (Appearance tab and Compendium) are readable again: the text sat under the faded item picture.\n- Send feedback is in Settings (and /tcf feedback) instead of the top of the window.\n- Test mode: a Remove fake cats button, and fake party cats go away when you leave a group." },
  { version = "1.5.0", highlight = "Class professions with crafted gear, party cats with a tap bonus, a fishing dock, 33 new cat skins and the Compendium.", text = "|cffffd100Professions by class|r\n- Your cat's class now picks its main profession. Warriors and Paladins get Mining with Blacksmithing. Rogues, Druids, Hunters and Shamans get Skinning with Leatherworking. Mages, Priests and Warlocks get Tailoring.\n- Each one is the same idle business with the same numbers under its own names. Mining has Veins, a Pickaxe and Foremen. Skinning has Hunting Grounds (real beasts from higher-level zones, from Barrens Plainstriders to Devilsaurs), a Skinning Knife and Trappers. Tailoring has Cloth Spots (Defias Hideout, Syndicate Camp, Bloodsail Camp and more), Shears and Scavengers.\n- Hunting Grounds and Cloth Spots show the real creatures in 3D.\n- Each class's profession keeps its own progress, and your hired helpers keep working, online and offline, even while your cat is a different class.\n- Herbalism, First Aid, Fishing and Cooking still unlock later for everyone, at the same Renown costs.\n- Existing characters keep their progress: on first login a cloth or leather class moves its Mining spots, tool level, upgrades, milestones and skill to its new profession, and its ore becomes cloth or leather of the same tier.\n\n|cffffd100Crafting real gear|r\n- Blacksmithing, Leatherworking and Tailoring craft real Classic gear with stats, 45 recipes each from skill 1 to 300. Blacksmiths make plate, mail, weapons and shields, leatherworkers make leather and mail, tailors make cloth armor.\n- Crafting skill rises the classic way: orange recipes always give a point, yellow often, green sometimes, grey never. Reaching 300 is a long-term goal of several weeks.\n- Recipes you can't make yet are listed with the skill they need, so you can see what comes next.\n- Every cosmetic recipe says \"Cosmetic only (no stats)\" in the recipe list, its tooltip and the Compendium. You can't craft a cosmetic you already own.\n- Leatherworking and Tailoring each get 5 cosmetic recipes and their own craftable cat skins.\n- Crafted gear goes into your current class's gear bag and its tooltip says which profession made it. It is never found as loot, and it sells for Trade Gold, not TapCoins.\n\n|cffffd100Play with friends|r\n- Friends in your party or raid who also have TapCatForever show up as small cats in a row beside yours. Hover one to see whose cat it is.\n- Your taps count 20% more with one of them and 10% more for each one after that, up to +50% with a full party: more tap progress, cat XP and TapCoins from tapping.\n- The addons find each other on their own, across realms, and reconnect after a reload or a fight.\n\n|cffffd100Fishing dock|r\n- The Fishing page is now a cartoon dock over a lake. Your cat sits on the dock with a fishing pole and the bobber floats on the water.\n- Once you hire a Fishing Buddy, he sits beside your cat with his own pole, and wears a fishing hat once he levels up.\n\n|cffffd100New cat skins|r\n- 33 new cat skins, each with its own fur pattern in the cartoon style.\n- In the Shop: Mittens, Tuxedo Cat, Cow Cat, Russian Blue, Dalmatian Cat, Tortoiseshell and Snowshoe (300-650 TapCoins), Bengal, Maine Coon and Strawberry Sweetheart (1,000-1,200), and Galaxy Cat (3,200).\n- Rare Adventure boss drops (2-5% per kill): Ragefire Cinder Cat, Defias Bandit Cat, Stone Watcher Cat, Maraudon Crystal Cat, Scarlet Crusader Cat, Wind-Up Clockwork Cat, Onyxian Whelpling Cat, Qiraji Scarab Cat and Patchwork Kitty.\n- Chest-only cats: Lucky Clover Cat and Rainbow Cat (Adventurer's Strongbox), Golden Treasure Cat and Diamond Cat (Heroic Cache).\n- Quest cats (Quest-Giver Cat, Ready-to-Turn-In Cat), expedition cats (Emberheart Cat, Runebound Cat), real dungeon and raid cats (Party Animal, Raid Leader Cat) and craftable cats.\n\n|cffffd100Compendium|r\n- A new Compendium window (button at the top of the main window, or /tcf compendium) lists every skin, cosmetic, tap effect, effect and piece of gear, what you own, and how to get the rest.\n\n|cffffd100Loot and gear|r\n- Gear and cosmetics you find no longer open a big loot box. They go straight into your bags and a small notice appears by your cat: hover it to compare with what you wear, click it to open the Gear or Appearance tab, right-click to dismiss. Opening a chest still plays the reel.\n- Every gear tooltip compares the item with what your cat is wearing, as a Power change.\n- \"Sell unequipped\" is now \"Sell junk\": it sells gear that would lower your Power and extra copies you can't wear. Upgrades are kept, even ones you need a higher level for.\n- Starter weapons fit the class: a bow for hunters, a dagger for rogues, a mace for paladins, priests and shamans, a sword for warriors and a staff for mages, warlocks and druids.\n\n|cffffd100Other|r\n- A short \"What's new\" note appears at the top of the window after a big update, and the full patch notes are in Settings (or /tcf news).\n- New Send feedback window (button at the top of the main window, in Settings, or /tcf feedback).\n- Enemies in Adventure are no longer cut off at the edges of their boxes.\n- Cloth now sells for the same as ore and leather." },
  { version = "1.4.0", highlight = nil, text = "|cffffd100More enemies in Adventure|r\n- Every zone, dungeon and raid now has its real Classic creatures: up to 16 different enemies per zone (335 in all, up from 56), with real models taken from a full Classic creature database. Molten Core goes from 2 creature types to 13, Naxxramas from 3 to 15, Elwynn Forest from 3 to 13.\n- More bosses now use their own real models instead of stand-ins.\n- A pack no longer has the same creature twice when the zone has enough variety.\n- Enemies play their death animation and fade out (including the last one in a pack and bosses), and killing blows show their spell effect.\n- Damage and healing numbers float above enemies instead of behind them, and the ability buttons flash when your cat uses an ability.\n\n|cffffd100Adventure fixes and balance|r\n- Fixed a bug that kept Divine Shield, Ice Block, Recklessness and other buffs up almost all the time and reset every cooldown at the start of each fight. Abilities now last and recharge as their tooltips say, so some raid bosses are harder.\n- Adventure chests are now based on time spent fighting: about one Cat Treat Pouch per 15-25 minutes in zones and dungeons, and one Adventurer's Strongbox per 30 minutes in raids, dropped by a boss. Trash no longer drops pouches.\n- Auto-advance off now really means \"keep farming this stage\": a lost fight retries the same stage. After 3 losses in a row your cat drops back to an easier pack. With Auto-advance on, a cat that loses at the start of a zone falls back to the previous zone.\n- Bandages in fights work again after their cooldown, instead of staying locked.\n\n|cffffd100Gear and chests|r\n- A chest's Rare or Epic roll no longer quietly turns into a green item; the chest looks a little wider for your level before dropping a quality.\n- Chests keep giving proper gear after your cat passes level 60.\n- Brand-new cats no longer get very strong endgame gear: items with no level requirement now need roughly their item level minus 5. Every class starts with a fair level-10 weapon.\n- Boss drops are always gear your class can wear. Blizzard's leftover test items are gone from loot.\n- Equipping a one-hander while wearing a two-hander now replaces the two-hander. With both ring or trinket slots full, Equip replaces the weaker one. The \"+power\" number is now correct in every case, and you can equip a second copy of a ring, trinket or one-hander.\n- Selling: tooltips say exactly what Sell does, you're asked before selling your only copy of a rare or epic, and \"Sell unequipped\" no longer stutters with a big bag.\n- Hovering gear previews it on your cat even when that slot has a cosmetic.\n- The Shop shows the real chest odds (90% gear, 10% cosmetic).\n\n|cffffd100Cartoon cat|r\n- Hunter bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons now show in your cat's paw, and capes show on its back in their own colours.\n- Gear that shares another slot's icon now draws in the right place (no more belts on helms or daggers from necklaces).\n- Floating effects bob smoothly and stay centred.\n- Scrolling over the cat zooms the camera again (hold Ctrl or Shift to resize or fade the cat).\n- The cat no longer leaves an invisible strip that blocked clicks, and it stays exactly where you put it after this update.\n\n|cffffd100Professions|r\n- Pickaxe swings on higher veins now pay a fair share of that vein's output instead of beating your whole business.\n- Mr. Pinchy's gold wish now gives about 10 minutes of what your mines make. Your fishing buddy finds treasure much less often than you do when you fish yourself, and lists offline finds in one line.\n- Cooking: ingredients taken from the pot before you cook now empty the pot (no more free dishes), Burnt Mess rarely raises your skill, and there's a new recipe to discover that uses Raptor Flesh.\n- First Aid: the Field Medic makes the best bandage you have cloth for, and stalled queues say what cloth they need.\n- Herbalism: clicking a locked plot no longer buys a different plot.\n\n|cffffd100Expeditions, quests and dungeons|r\n- Short expeditions are now mainly for XP and TapCoins; chests come mostly from the long ones. Tooltips show the real chest odds.\n- You're told when a party gets back (on the cat, and in chat if chat messages are on), even if it came back while you were offline.\n- Quests track progress correctly across your characters and can't show negative numbers. Boss quests take about as long as the others.\n- Real dungeon and raid chests: re-entering after stepping out or a wipe continues the same run. Each dungeon gives a chest once a day, each raid once a week, and up to 2 dungeon chests a day across your characters. You're told when a run gives no chest.\n\n|cffffd100Account and characters|r\n- Achievement rewards (cosmetics and cat skins such as Mr. Bigglesworth) now appear on all your characters, and you keep them after \"Reset this character\".\n- \"Citizen of Azeroth\" counts heritage pieces from all your characters, and \"Completionist\" can reach 100% again.\n- Each character has its own Daily Wares.\n- Playing past midnight gives you the new day's treat and keeps your streak.\n- Slash commands and replies to your own clicks always show in chat, even with \"Chat messages\" turned off; that setting now only mutes passive notices.\n\n|cffffd100Interface|r\n- The Treasure Bag is wider so chest names aren't hidden, the loot box switches to a new reel's item instead of hiding it, and \"Open all\" no longer freezes the game with a big pile of chests.\n- Achievements show their cat-skin rewards, and the Appearance and Shop pages no longer overlap their buttons." },
  { version = "1.3.3", highlight = nil, text = "- The loot box only pops up while the TapCatForever window or Treasure Bag is open; otherwise drops show as a small note above the cat.\n- \"Sell spare copies\" is now \"Sell unequipped\": it says it sells every piece of gear the cat isn't wearing, and asks you to confirm with the item count and TapCoins.\n- Loot box: Open another, Equip, OK to all and OK no longer overlap.\n- Welcome: the tip on the second page no longer hides behind the Back button." },
  { version = "1.3.2", highlight = nil, text = "- Adventure: you can move on to the next zone as soon as you beat the current one, whatever your level (Auto-advance still waits for the right level).\n- Every boss drops a guaranteed piece of its real loot the first time you beat it.\n- Adventure shows what the next zone needs next to the zone arrows (clear the final boss, or the level required).\n- Shorter welcome: two pages, the logo with your tapping cat, then a picture grid of what to do.\n- Pickaxe swings now grow with the deposit: each swing is worth half a second of everything that vein produces (all your mines there, with milestones and upgrades), never less than a quarter of one mine's cycle. Pickaxe levels add 15% each." },
  { version = "1.3.1", highlight = nil, text = "- Chests now give real gear 90% of the time (cosmetics 10%).\n- Cosmetics are clearly marked: a COSMETIC tag and \"appearance only, no stats\" in the loot box and tooltips, and a purple badge on the chest reel. Gear shows a GEAR tag." },
  { version = "1.3.0", highlight = nil, text = "- Hand-drawn Adventure backgrounds for all 28 zones, dungeons and raids.\n- Chest opening reel: possible loot spins by and lands on your reward (can be turned off in Settings).\n- Mining: idle veins say \"Click to mine a cycle\" and pulse; the pickaxe is labelled \"By hand\".\n- Spell effects in Adventure: your cat's abilities now show as they're cast: fireballs, frostbolts, shadow bolts, lightning, arrows, slashes, falling Blizzard and Rain of Fire, heals, shield bubbles and stun stars.\n- Ability bar under the fight with every learned ability and its cooldown counting down.\n- Chests now only give cosmetics your current class can wear (its own sets or universal items).\n- Welcome tour on first login (also in Settings and /tcf welcome), with a cartoon version of the TapCatForever logo.\n- Hand mining pays much less: a quarter of one mine's cycle per swing, with a 25% chance of ore." },
  { version = "1.2.1", highlight = nil, text = "- Developer test shortcuts are now password-locked." },
  { version = "1.2.0", highlight = nil, text = "- New cartoon cat: a hand-drawn sticker-style cat with expressions (happy, blink, sparkle, focus). It replaces the pixel cat.\n- Every visible item has its own drawing: all ~4,500 helms, chests, belts, necklaces, rings, weapons, shields and off-hand items, each drawn from its in-game icon (785 unique looks).\n- Dual-wielded weapons appear in both paws; shields, books and orbs in the left paw.\n- Hovering an item now shows your cat wearing it (instead of your WoW character).\n- Treasure Bag: \"All\" button per chest type and \"Open everything\".\n- The level and XP text now sit above the cat (Settings: \"Text above the cat\"). Chat messages and sounds now start off.\n- Mining veins only run when you start them or a foreman works them (key presses no longer restart them).\n- Each cat class has its own gear bag: gear found on one class no longer shows up for the others (an old shared bag is split once: worn items stay with their class, the rest go to the class you are playing).\n- All cosmetics redrawn for the cartoon cat: every hat, chest, cape and wings, weapon, off-hand, accessory and racial heritage item (78 designs), tinted in each item's own colours. Fur patterns recolour the cat's markings.\n- Fur patterns and special skins drawn properly: tabby, tuxedo, star blaze, calico, Siamese points and leopard markings; tiger stripes, star spots, Mechanocat plates, Skeletal Cat bones, the War Lion's mane and coloured eyes.\n- Mining: one pickaxe for every vein with an endless upgrade (+15% per hand-mined click per level, an extra ore every 15 levels). Clicking the pickaxe shows what you mined; it has a 1.5s swing cooldown (shorter with upgrades, down to 0.75s).\n- Herbalism: seeds show their price (or the skill they need), the garden says what you're planting and what it costs, and failed plants explain why.\n- Professions page: buttons no longer miss clicks (the page was redrawing its views underneath the mouse).\n- Cooking: spice buttons show their price, and the tooltip explains what spices are for and which known dishes use them.\n- Expeditions give XP to every cat that went (5 XP per minute away, half on a failure).\n- Tap Effects: a new cosmetic slot. A little burst pops from the paw on every tap: 17 to collect (Dust Puffs and Paw Prints up to Holy Light and Rainbow Stars), from chests and the shop.\n- Paws move further on each tap. The chest badge next to the cat is gone (open chests from the Treasure Bag button in the window).\n- Settings: \"Reset this character\" and \"Reset ALL progress\".\n- Real WoW gear: 8,661 real Classic items with their real stats (Strength, Stamina, Armor, weapon DPS, crit, spell power...), drop sources and drop chances. 17 gear slots per class (Head to Ranged), Classic armor and weapon rules per class, and the cat wears its real gear (cosmetics still override the look).\n- Adventure rebuilt around Azeroth: 28 real zones, dungeons and raids in level order (Elwynn Forest, Deadmines, Scarlet Monastery... Molten Core, Blackwing Lair, Naxxramas) with their real bosses and real loot tables. Packs of 1-3 enemies shown as 3D creature models, over each dungeon's own artwork. Zones unlock by class level; raids need raid gear.\n- Class abilities: 9-10 real abilities per class (Heroic Strike, Fireball, Frost Nova, Shadow Word: Pain, Holy Light...) bought with TapCoins and used automatically in fights.\n- Expeditions: send a party of 3 cats away for 15 minutes to 24 hours (even offline); they come back with TapCoins, chests and gear.\n- Professions: five professions that each play differently, all with an idle mode, unlocked with Renown (selling your business): Mining (free: an idle tycoon of veins with foremen and milestones, plus your own pickaxe to mine by hand), Herbalism (5 Renown: a garden whose plots grow in real time; key presses water it; a gardener harvests and replants, and rare Black Lotus mutations), First Aid (20: cloth from Adventure becomes the 10 Classic bandages, which heal your cat mid-fight; a field medic and cloth contract automate it), Fishing (60: a bobber mini-game across five real fishing spots with Mr. Pinchy's wishes; a fishing buddy catches on his own) and Cooking (150: experiment with fish, meat, herbs and spices to discover 12 Classic dishes that give Well Fed buffs; a sous-chef cooks for you). Materials still craft exclusive effects and cats.\n- Cat skins: a new Skin slot that restyles the whole cat: Striped Frostsaber, Striped Nightsaber, Spotted Frostsaber, Black Panther, Darkmoon Kitty, Winterspring Frostsaber, Mechanical Kitty, Fel Kitty, Golden Lion and Spectral Tiger (bought with TapCoins in the Appearance tab, or rarely found in Heroic Caches), plus Swift Zulian Tiger (High Priest Thekal) and Skeletal Cat (Baron Rivendare) as rare Adventure boss drops.\n- Racial heritage: buy your character's race accessory in the Shop (Orc tusks, Tauren horns, Night Elf ears, Gnome goggles, Skyborne feathers and more); it can be hidden in Settings.\n- Real dungeons: below level 20 you get a Cat Treat Pouch, from 20 an Adventurer's Strongbox (chance of a Heroic Cache, higher from 50); raids give a Heroic Cache.\n- Chests now hold real gear (65%) or cosmetics (35%). Epic and Legendary gear is deliberately rare.\n- Appearance only shows cosmetics you've unlocked.\n- Gear try-on: hover gear to see your cat wearing it.\n- Per-character progress: gear, cosmetics, skins, chests, professions, cat levels, abilities and Adventure belong to each character; TapCoins, quests, streak and achievements are shared.\n- Adventure waits for you to press Start; only the selected class's cat fights. Rewards are mostly chests. Every enemy is shown as a model, and Elwynn Forest and Westfall have painted scenes.\n- Loot from chests and bosses suits your class (no caster staves for Warriors). The loot box shows what else is waiting and has \"OK to all\".\n- More to collect: 104 colour variants of 13 effect styles, and cat skins from tabbies to sabers and achievement cats like Mr. Bigglesworth.\n- New \"Text size\" setting, separate from cat size, so a tiny cat can keep readable text.\n- New quests and achievements for gear, expeditions and crafting.\n\n- Adventure: a new idle game tab. Your cat fights through 12 tiers of classic zones, dungeons and raids (Elwynn Forest to Naxxramas, then endless Heroic tiers), using the gear equipped on the current class. Every key press lands a bonus paw strike. Bosses drop cosmetics.\n- Quests: 3 daily quests (TapCoins + a Cat Treat Pouch each) and a weekly quest (TapCoins + an Adventurer's Strongbox).\n- Real dungeon and raid rewards: boss kills pay TapCoins; finishing a dungeon gives an Adventurer's Strongbox, a raid gives a Heroic Cache.\n- Treasure Bag for unopened chests, and a loot reveal box that shows what you got.\n- Per-class levels: each class levels up on its own, starting at 1.\n- Gear slots around the cat in the window: click a slot to choose its item, right-click to empty it.\n- A / left arrow and left mouse tap the left paw; D / right arrow and right mouse tap the right paw; other keys alternate.\n- Weapons, shields and other held items now sit in front of the paws.\n- The cat in the window no longer taps on its own.\n- TapCoins are scarcer: 1 per 50 key presses; quests and Adventure are the main income. Daily wares show 3 items." },
  { version = "1.1.1", highlight = nil, text = "- First CurseForge release (same content as 1.1.0)." },
  { version = "1.1.0", highlight = nil, text = "- Targets World of Warcraft: Forever (interface 16001) and its modern addon API.\n- Uses modern APIs only (C_AddOns, class icon atlases, missing-icon fallback).\n- Adds a page under Options > AddOns.\n- Never reads game values that may be \"secret\" in combat; the cast fallback uses whichever spellcast event the client provides." },
  { version = "1.0.0", highlight = nil, text = "- First release: the tapping cat, 9 classes, 612 cosmetics, TapCoins, daily shop, treasure chests, 43 achievements, account-wide progression." },
}
